{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoJJQVZy35sDK9YEBzu3vM","type":"tool_result","content":"569:This is the third sighting of the same light. An Ingress with no Ingress controller routes nothing. A NetworkPolicy on a CNI plugin that doesn't implement policy blocks nothing. A StorageClass with no running provisioner creates nothing. Each time, the object exists, `kubectl get` shows it, `kubectl describe` shows a sensible spec, and nothing happens, because the object was always only ever a request addressed to a component that has to be separately installed and running.\n571:You will see it a fourth time in §5, and by then the recognition should be automatic.\n871:That is the same light, the fourth time. And once you have seen it four times, you stop asking \"is the object there?\" and start asking \"is the *component* there?\", which is the question Chapter 10 said you would know to ask."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d9b807e-74b1-4e23-a469-c2ab5f0edd1f","uuid":"756160cf-5eb4-4e43-ada1-0f87f32c28f1","timestamp":"2026-08-25T07:30:54.222Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"569:This is the third sighting of the same light. An Ingress with no Ingress controller routes nothing. A NetworkPolicy on a CNI plugin that doesn't implement policy blocks nothing. A StorageClass with no running provisioner creates nothing. Each time, the object exists, `kubectl get` shows it, `kubectl describe` shows a sensible spec, and nothing happens, because the object was always only ever a request addressed to a component that has to be separately installed and running.\n571:You will see it a fourth time in §5, and by then the recognition should be automatic.\n871:That is the same light, the fourth time. And once you have seen it four times, you stop asking \"is the object there?\" and start asking \"is the *component* there?\", which is the question Chapter 10 said you would know to ask.","numLines":3,"totalLines":3}}
